  "text": "\r\n         Town of Milford, NH - Town Clerk \r\n     Skip to main content \r\nDepartments \nMain Menu  /  Departments \nDepartments \nAll Departments \nADA Compliance \nAmbulance \nAssessing \nBuilding Safety \nCommunity Development \nCommunity Media \nFinance \nFire Department \nHealth Department \nHuman Resources \nInformation Technology \nLibrary \nEmergency Management \nPlanning and GIS \nPolice Department \nPublic Works \nRecreation \nRecycling & Transfer Station \nStormwater Management \nTax Collection \nTown Administrator \nTown Clerk \nWater Utilities \nWelfare Department \nBoards \nMain Menu  /  Boards \nBoards \nAll Boards \nArtWalk Committee \nBudget Advisory Committee \nCemetery Trustees \nCIP Citizens Advisory Committee \nConservation Commission \nEconomic Development Advisory Council \nEnergy Advisory Committee \nEthics Committee \nGranite Town Media Advisory Committee \nHeritage Commission \nJoint Loss Management Committee \nLibrary Trustees \nMACC Base \nMaster Plan Steering Committee \nPlanning Board \nRecreation Commission \nRecycling Committee \nSelect Board \nTraffic Safety Committee \nTrustees of the Trust Fund \nVietnam Memorial Committee \nWater and Sewer Commissioners \nZoning Board of Adjustement \n250th Celebration Committee \nTown Government \nMain Menu  /  Town Government \nTown Government \nAbout Milford \nDepartments \nBoards \nElected Officials \nEmployment \nMinutes & Agendas \nActive Projects \nMunicipal Codes \nMaps / GIS Mapping \nContact Us \nResidents \nMain Menu  /  Residents \nResidents \nPermits, Forms & Links \nDepartment Directory \nUtility & Service Providers \nCommunity Power \nE Services & Payments \nVolunteer Opportunities \nSchools \nLibrary \nCemeteries \nNews & Public Notices \nCommunity Calendar \nBusiness \nMain Menu  /  Business \nBusiness \nLocal Business Organizations \nStarting a Business \nState & Regional Resources                                  \r\n                             About \r\n                             News  \r\n                             Staff \r\n                             Resources \r\nTown Clerk \r\n                             Town Clerk \r\nAbout \nThe duties and responsibilities of a town clerk are numerous and varied. There is no one place in the statutes to find a list of the duties for this position; rather, the duties can be found throughout many statutes such as motor vehicle laws, election laws, vital statistics, planning and land use laws, libraries and the budget law.  \nTown Official \nUnlike the tax collector, there is no provision in the law to allow a town clerk to be appointed. Thus, all town clerks must be elected and thereby must also be residents in the town they serve. City clerks, however, are appointed by the city council and are subject to the provisions of the city charter. These distinctions aside, most of the duties described below apply to city clerks as well as town clerks. \nAs a town official, the town clerk is not an employee of the town. The clerk may set his or her own office hours and take what vacation and sick time they feel they can, while still providing the service their constituents expect. However, this does not mean that there is no oversight of the position by the Select Board. While there is no direct supervision of the town clerk by the Select Board in the way that town employees are supervised, cooperation and a spirit of teamwork on the part of all town officials is essential. Only by working together will the goal of serving the town to the best of their abilities be achieved. \nThe town clerk submits his or her budget request to the Select Board for their consideration who then submit it the budget committee, if there is one. Within the budget request, the town clerk may include compensation, monies to attend training, and other items necessary to run the office. The legislative body has ultimate decision-making power over all budget requests presented at the annual meeting. Thus, if the Select Board or Budget Committee recommend a budget for the town clerk’s office that the clerk disagrees with, he or she can take the issue up with the voters at the annual meeting. \nlinks \nE-Reg \nDog Licensing  \nVital Records \ncontent \nHours of Operation: \nMon, Wed, Thurs 7:30 am to 5:30 pm Tues: 7:30 am to 6:30 pm CLOSED ON FRIDAY  \nPhone: \n(603) 249-0650 \nFax: \n(603) 673-2273 \nAddress: \nFoyer of main entrance to Milford Town Hall - Nashua Street. \n1 Union Square \nNews  \nNews and Announcements \nPosts \nStaff \nStaff Contacts \nPeople \nResources \nResources \nResources              \r\n1 Union Square, Milford, NH 03055 \n6032490600  |  web@milford.nh.gov \nPowered By  Munibit  | © 2026 Terms  |  Privacy  |  Notifications  |  Accessibility Login                  \r\nSection Tools \r\nHello  \r\nWhat is a Passkey? \n                Imagine signing into your account as easily as unlocking your phone—no more worrying about remembering or typing a password. A passkey is a secure digital key that uses the safety features in your device to keep your account protected. It’s designed to be both simple to use and highly secure. \n                Ready to experience a simpler, safer sign-in? Click the button above to create your passkey now. \r\nSign Up for Notifications! \r\n             Do not show again \r\nFill out the following fields. \n                     Activate notifications by clicking or tapping on the verification messages we send. Completing the verification process confirms your consent. Notification categories can be edited later from an email message footer. \r\n ",
